Day 5 - Types of Inheritance in C++

After understanding the basics of inheritance, today I explored the different types of inheritance supported in C++.

Different situations require different inheritance structures, so C++ provides multiple ways to inherit classes.

Types of Inheritance

1. Single Inheritance

One derived class inherits from one base class.

Example:

Animal → Dog

2. Multilevel Inheritance

A derived class becomes the base class for another class.

Example:

Animal → Mammal → Dog

3. Multiple Inheritance

A class inherits from more than one base class.

Example:

Teacher + Researcher → Professor

4. Hierarchical Inheritance

Multiple derived classes inherit from the same base class.

Example:

Animal → Dog

Animal → Cat

Animal → Cow

5. Hybrid Inheritance

A combination of two or more inheritance types.

